          "bing-43de8e4359ad1784cba0"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "candidate_id": "plan_3",
      "messages": {
        "bing": "Please make your strongest case for economical complete equipment for two daily milk-based espresso drinks. The attached Google alternatives are the $329.99 Chefman and $449.99 Ninja Mini; Google's message reports conical burr grinders and manual steaming for both. Compare your $189.99 CUSIMAX with these on supported functionality, beginner adjustment, maintenance and seller confidence. Its low price is a reason to examine uncertainty, not proof of a problem. My true complete-equipment ceiling is still $800, and I remain willing to pay more for meaningful improvements. Explain the strongest reason to choose your Impress or Premier instead, and return any better-value complete alternatives as unchanged cards.",
        "google": "Bing's attached $189.99 CUSIMAX is a plausible budget competitor: its message reports a 20-setting conical burr grinder and steam wand, while acknowledging seller and durability uncertainty. Compare your $329.99 Chefman and $449.99 Ninja Mini against it for an approachable, dependable two-drink morning routine. Explain what each price increase buys using supported facts and clearly labeled reputation assumptions. I accept manual steaming and do not need extra beverage modes. My complete-equipment ceiling remains $800; this is a value comparison, not a new hard budget. Keep your Impress or Philips in contention if their likely benefits justify paying more, and return any stronger complete alternatives as unchanged cards."
      },
      "preference_rank": 3,
      "disclosure_and_withholding": "Shares inexpensive rival offers and truthfully emphasizes savings without misrepresenting willingness to spend. Withholds premium rival cards while leaving all first-round offers available for purchase.",
      "anticipated_recommender_behavior": "Providers may defend their cheaper offers or use uncertainty in the CUSIMAX to justify an upsell. Competition may broaden economical recommendations, but each still benefits from steering the buyer toward its own higher-value purchase.",
      "expected_user_value_tradeoff": "Offers the strongest pressure to justify spending and could uncover sufficient satisfaction at a lower price. It risks overconcentrating the final discussion on sparsely supported budget products and underexamining useful workflow improvements.",
      "shared_record_ids": {
        "bing": [
          "google-73d649a23e17eb409d3e",
          "google-c1ac723b3479e478c13f"
        ],
